<!--
  Card face for the Stack (tilt) fan.

  20dp corners, measured off a One UI 8 tilt stack at 420dpi: the front card's left edge only
  becomes straight ~53px below its top edge, and solving the circle for two sampled rows both give
  r ≈ 53px ≈ 20dp. (Noticeably tighter than it looks by eye — the cards read as very round because
  they are narrow, not because the radius is large.)

  The fill is only ever seen through a task with no snapshot, where RecentsCardBinder centres the
  app icon on it, and in the corners the snapshot's own square corners leave behind. A near-black
  neutral so neither case flashes bright against the blurred wallpaper.

  Doubles as the outline source: the face sets clipToOutline, so this radius is what rounds the
  snapshot and what shapes the card's elevation shadow.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="#FF1B1B1B" />
    <corners android:radius="20dp" />
</shape>
